00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.100
So you might have a back end
binary, a front end binary,

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.060
and so on.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.080
And those would be in command
back end, command front end,

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:55.212
and so on.

00:08:55.212 --> 00:08:57.420
In this case, I'm just going
to write one web server,

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.580
so I'm doing just in
the command directory.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:04.540
So in here we have package main.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:07.540
Going to write a func main.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.240
And this has a few steps.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.400
One-- we're going to check what
port should we be listening on.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:19.300
So the App Engine runtime
will set the port environment

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.850
variable to the port that
you should be listening on

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.680
for your HTTP server.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.350
Other than that, whatever
setup you need to do

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.880
