00:10:56.173 --> 00:10:57.590
We don't want to
lesson on a port.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:00.360
We want to lesson on
some end point, which is,

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.300
we'll say /hello.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.840
Here we're listening on
some port, default marks,

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:09.462
close fatal, and there we go.

00:11:09.462 --> 00:11:11.920
So at the top here, we have a
few imports from the standard

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:16.340
library, and we have
this example.com/hello.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.455
And that's really it.

00:11:19.455 --> 00:11:21.080
And this is how you
would write an HTTP

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.167
